# Rust build output (matches the root target/ AND nested ones, e.g. the vendored RPG grammar)
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Built graph databases (created by `wicked-estate index`) + SQLite WAL/SHM sidecars
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
# Exception: versioned v0.12.x fixture databases committed as test fixtures
!crates/wicked-estate-mcp/tests/fixtures/*_v*.db
!crates/wicked-estate-mcp/tests/fixtures/*_v*.db.memext
.code-intel/
.wicked-estate/

# Embedding model caches (downloaded by the model2vec / fastembed features)
.fastembed_cache/
.cache/

# Internal reference material (not for publication)
/.reference

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# NOTE: Cargo.lock IS committed — wicked-estate ships as a binary (reproducible builds).
# NOTE: crates/we-extract/vendor/tree-sitter-rpg/src/parser.c IS committed — vendored grammar source.

# Estate store artifacts written beside a site build. The `*.db` rules above do NOT
# match these -- the suffix comes AFTER .db (wicked-estate.db.mem, .db.knowledge-wal),
# so `git add -A` in site/ would happily commit a local database.
#
# Scoped to site/ deliberately. Rooted `*.db.mem*` would apply repo-wide and sit BELOW the
# fixture un-ignores at the top of this file, and later rules win -- so it would be a live
# hazard for any future crates/**/fixtures/*_v*.db.memext. (Those fixtures are already
# governed by their own nested .gitignore, which ignores *.db.memext and un-ignores the one
# checked-in file; this scoping keeps the two from ever interacting.)
site/*.db.mem*
site/*.db.knowledge*
